    // Deploy the CEP47 token contract with the provided initial parameters
    match cep47::deploy(token_name, token_symbol, initial_supply, decimal_places, entry_points) {
        Ok(_) => runtime::ret(()) // Contract deployment successful
        Err(err) => runtime::revert(ApiError::from(err)) // Contract deployment failed
    }
}
```

In the solution, the deployment function is completed by adding the necessary code to set the initial supply, decimal places, and any other required parameters for the CEP47 token deployment. The `get_named_arg` function is used to retrieve the initial supply, decimal places, token name, and token symbol from the contract call parameters. The `cep47::deploy` function is then called with the provided initial parameters, and the result is handled to either return successfully or revert with an error in case of failure.

