### Problem:
You are tasked with creating a function that processes a given array of file paths and extracts the unique base URLs from those paths. The file paths are in the format of PHP echo statements within an HTML file, as shown in the code snippet below:

```php
<?php
$filePaths = [
    '<?php echo Yii::app()->theme->baseUrl;?>/assets/js/jquery-ui.min.js',
    '<?php echo Yii::app()->theme->baseUrl;?>/assets/css/style.css',
    '<?php echo Yii::app()->theme->baseUrl;?>/assets/js/custom.js',
    '<?php echo Yii::app()->theme->baseUrl;?>/assets/images/logo.png',
];
?>
```

Your task is to implement a function `extractBaseUrls($filePaths)` that takes an array of file paths as input and returns an array of unique base URLs extracted from those paths. The base URL is the part of the path enclosed within the PHP echo statement, i.e., `<?php echo ...;?>`.

Function signature: `function extractBaseUrls(array $filePaths): array`

Example:
Input:
```
$filePaths = [
    '<?php echo Yii::app()->theme->baseUrl;?>/assets/js/jquery-ui.min.js',
    '<?php echo Yii::app()->theme->baseUrl;?>/assets/css/style.css',
    '<?php echo Yii::app()->theme->baseUrl;?>/assets/js/custom.js',
    '<?php echo Yii::app()->theme->baseUrl;?>/assets/images/logo.png',
];
```
Output:
```
['Yii::app()->theme->baseUrl']
```

Assume that the input array will always contain valid file paths in the specified format.

### Solution:
```php
function extractBaseUrls(array $filePaths): array {
    $baseUrls = [];
    foreach ($filePaths as $path) {
        preg_match('/<\?php echo (.*?); ?>/', $path, $matches);
        if (isset($matches[1])) {
            $baseUrls[] = trim($matches[1], " '");
        }
    }
    return array_unique($baseUrls);
}

// Test the function
