   - `name`: a string representing the name of the item.
   - `price`: a number representing the price of the item.
2. `discountThreshold`: a number representing the total cost threshold above which a discount is applicable.

The function should calculate the total cost of the items in the shopping cart. If the total cost exceeds the `discountThreshold`, a 10% discount should be applied to the total cost.

The function should return the total cost after applying any applicable discount.

Example:
```javascript
const items = [
  { name: 'Shirt', price: 25 },
  { name: 'Jeans', price: 40 },
  { name: 'Shoes', price: 50 }
];
const discountThreshold = 100;

calculateTotalCost(items, discountThreshold); // Output: 108 (25 + 40 + 50 - 10% discount)
```

### Solution:
```javascript
function calculateTotalCost(items, discountThreshold) {
  let totalCost = items.reduce((acc, item) => acc + item.price, 0);
  if (totalCost > discountThreshold) {
    totalCost *= 0.9; // Apply 10% discount
  }
